{#
  Jonson CTA beat — the ways-to-connect moment inside a response ([[contact]]).

  ONE BUTTON, for everyone, VIP or not. Its label is `jonsonCtaButtonText` on the
  globals single — ONE label for every visitor, deliberately, rather than the contact
  single's question re-asked per purpose: this button follows a reply that has just
  made the case, so it continues the conversation instead of opening a new one (that
  copy stays on the contact page and the panel).

  `offerRoutes` — set only when the beat was added by CODE rather than marked by the
  model (the engagement-floor branch in AskController). That difference is the whole
  reason this block exists. A model-marked [[contact]] arrives under a sentence the
  model wrote, and for a VIP that sentence already carries the call and WhatsApp links;
  the floor's beat arrives under an answer written without any contact moment at all,
  so the routes have nowhere to be. This line is that sentence, written by us because
  nobody else did.

  IT HAS TO STAND ON ITS OWN. It opened "Or reach me directly", which reads as the
  back half of a sentence — and the sentence it was continuing is whatever the model
  happened to end on, which is never the same twice and is often already an invitation
  to talk. A line appended to an answer cannot lean on the line above it.

  LINKS, NOT MORE BUTTONS. A row of buttons mid-conversation reads as a form; a line
  saying "call me on <number>" reads as a person saying it. Same reasoning as the
  prose, and the same [[tel:]] / wa.me URLs, from the same CTAs.

  Expects: contact — the contact single entry.
  Optional: offerRoutes — bool.
#}
{% if contact is defined and contact %}
    {# Not a CTA switched off for tools (isExcludedFromTools) — the same exclusion the
       case-content form applies to craft.frontend.ctas(). #}
    {% set routes = (offerRoutes ?? false) ? craft.frontend.doorCtas()|filter(c => not (c.isExcludedFromTools ?? false)) : [] %}
    {# The label is Jon's, from the globals single — same place the footer and contact
       panel read their copy from, fetched the same way they fetch it. Falls back to the
       label this button carried before the field existed, so an empty field is a button
       with sensible words on it rather than an empty pill. #}
    {% set globals = craft.entries().section('globals').one() %}
    {% set ctaLabel = (globals ? (globals.jonsonCtaButtonText ?? '')|trim : '') ?: 'Let’s talk more' %}
    <div class="c-ctas c-ctas--jonson">
        {% if routes|length %}
            {# A sentence: "Reach me directly: Telephone +33…, Send me a WhatsApp or Send
               me an email". The labels are the CTAs' titles exactly as Jon typed them in
               the CP, capitals and all — lowercasing them is what once turned "Send me a
               WhatsApp" into "send me a whatsapp", a brand name spelled wrong by us. A
               phone number is its own label, introduced as "Telephone": someone reading
               on a desktop cannot tap it, and someone who wants to save it has to see it.

               Only routes with a usable URL count, so the commas and the "or" are placed
               over THOSE — filtered first, not skipped mid-loop, or a dropped last route
               would leave the sentence ending on a comma. #}
            {% set links = [] %}
            {% for cta in routes %}
                {# safeUrl strips the invisible Unicode a pasted phone number brings with
                   it; see _components/ctas.twig for the whole story. #}
                {% set href = craft.frontend.safeUrl(cta.ctaUrl.url ?? null) %}
                {% if href %}
                    {% set links = links|merge([{href: href, tel: href starts with 'tel:', title: cta.title}]) %}
                {% endif %}
            {% endfor %}
            {% if links|length %}
                <p class="c-ctas__routes">Reach me directly:
                    {%- for link in links %}
                        {{- loop.first ? ' ' : (loop.last ? ' or ' : ', ') -}}
                        {% if link.tel %}Telephone <a class="c-jonson__link" href="{{ link.href }}">{{ link.href|replace({'tel:': ''}) }}</a>
                        {%- else %}<a class="c-jonson__link" href="{{ link.href }}">{{ link.title }}</a>{% endif %}
                    {%- endfor %}
                </p>
            {% endif %}
        {% endif %}
        {% include '_components/button.twig' with {
            label: ctaLabel,
            href:  siteUrl('contact'),
            size:  'md',
        } only %}
    </div>
{% endif %}
